 | R-Z14  | The app survives a full disk. (1) A store write the disk refuses is rejected with STORE_WRITE_FAILED, kept in memory (up to 64 MB) and retried with growing waits (5 s up to 60 s); the store is then degraded, and past the limit new writes are refused with STORE_FULL; when the disk takes the data again the queue is written in order and the store recovers, and flush() never answers while data is only queued. (2) The logger never throws: lines it cannot write are counted and one log_lines_dropped line follows when writing works again, and the crash handlers cannot fail while reporting. (3) A free-space guard skips the snapshot, compaction and backup with reason low_disk instead of half-writing them; the backup route answers 507 with code LOW_DISK. (4) Temporary files left by a failed write are removed. (5) /api/health reports the free disk space (or null when the platform cannot say) and the store state (degraded, queued bytes). (6) The page shows a dismissible banner "Disk almost full" under 1 GiB free or while writes fail, and none when the free space is unknown. (7) Telegram: the account counter and each channel counter never move past an update whose store write failed; the next catch-up fetches it again. The store's media folder and its files are now private (0700/0600) like logs and archives. Limit: a live Telegram update whose store write fails more than about 1 s after it arrived can be lost if the server crashes in that window. Not checked against real Telegram.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | `js/src/storage/write-queue.js`, `js/src/storage/lino-store.js`, `js/src/storage/disk-space.js`